"I was following the method described in the Ring background map tutorial to generate the distribution of significances. When calculating the corresponding distributions for the OFF bins, the applied approach (which multiplies the exclusion mask on the significance map before generating the histogram) doesn’t remove/ignore the excluded pixels but simply sets their significance to 0. In the tutorial this is only visible when you know what to look for, but I’ve rerun the code and increased the exclusion region size, and then it becomes obvious. I’d therefore suggest to update this tutorial by ignoring resp. removing those pixels from the distribution."","created_at":"2024-10-21T14:20:58Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T14:20:58Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gammapy/gammapy/pulls/5516/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gammapy/gammapy/pulls/5516/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gammapy/gammapy/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gammapy/gammapy/issues/5516/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gammapy/gammapy/statuses/da8a895862f368b8597b1c821964156fff2ced8e","head":{"label":"AtreyeeS:tutorial","ref":"tutorial","sha":"da8a895862f368b8597b1c821964156fff2ced8e","user":{"login":"AtreyeeS","id":32677370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjc3Mzcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32677370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtreyeeS","html_url":"https://github.com/AtreyeeS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtreyeeS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtreyeeS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtreyeeS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AtreyeeS/starred{/owner}{/rep